8612594?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/warkenji","html_url":"https://github.com/warkenji","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/warkenji/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/warkenji/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/warkenji/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/warkenji/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/warkenji/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/warkenji/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/warkenji/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/warkenji/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/warkenji/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-19T15:19:23Z","updated_at":"2025-12-21T06:58:40Z","body":"The issue appears to be that ColorParameter converts sRGB input into linear when entering the shader, and then outputs it back to sRGB at the albedo stage. In contrast, ColorConstant provides a raw value that is already in sRGB, but it gets reconverted to sRGB again, leading to an inconsistency.\nTo fix it, you simply need to connect the output of ColorConstant directly to the ColorFunc SRGBToLinear node (Godot 4.4+).\n\n[visual_shader_color_constant_parameter_bug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/24260750/visual_shader_color_constant_parameter_bug.zip)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3675465113/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]